     t_onReady(function() {t_onFuncLoad('t491_init',function() {t491_init('2463201481');});}); #rec2463201481 .t-card__title{font-size:20px;font-family:var(--t-text-font,Arial);font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;}@media screen and (max-width:480px),(orientation:landscape) and (max-height:480px){#rec2463201481 .t-card__title{font-size:14px;}}#rec2463201481 .t-card__descr{font-size:20px;font-family:var(--t-text-font,Arial);}@media screen and (max-width:480px),(orientation:landscape) and (max-height:480px){#rec2463201481 .t-card__descr{font-size:14px;}}          Eridan Audio Antares R2R DAC Total*: $4500 Buy Now   Perfect Matches This proprietary multibit DAC architecture is engineered to deliver unmatched musicality and depth. For the ultimate playback presentation, we highly recommend this synergy:   Antares R2R DAC  +   Konstantin Audio Interconnect Cables  +   Demograf Icarus AC Power Cables  = Ultimate Synergy  Add recommended synergy components to get 5% OFF your total order.     Key Features Specification Versions Options     Revolutionary "HumanDAC 36.6" Technology This proprietary multibit DAC architecture performs true "Bit-to-Bit" conversion without any digital pre-processing—no filters, CPLD, ALTERA, or MAX chips are used. This purist approach completely preserves the integrity, dynamics, and timing of the original source signal. Innovative "No Amp" Topology The DAC generates an unprecedented internal voltage level of 36.6V at the exact moment of analog signal birth—up to 1,000 times higher than industry norms. This immense output births the "No Amp" technology, entirely removing the need for voltage amplification stages and their inherent distortion or coloration. This 36.6V output is robust enough to deliver 40W into a 4-ohm load and flawlessly powers the dedicated headphone output. Basic vs. Ultra Editions The Antares Basic utilizes 2 DAC chips per channel, establishing the formidable baseline of the HumanDAC architecture with standard RCA outputs (2.5V amplitude). The Antares Ultra is a massive leap forward, employing 8 DAC chips per channel. Running in balanced mode via XLR, it engages all 8 chips to deliver a 4x increase in scale, dynamic range, and detail over the Basic version. Unbalanced RCA connection on the Ultra utilizes 4 chips per channel. Pristine Power & Versatile Connectivity Equipped with Eridan Audio's proprietary custom power supply, every component receives impeccably clean power free from ripple and noise. The DAC features three digital inputs (USB, Optical, Coaxial) and comprehensive outputs including fixed-level, variable-level, and a dedicated 6.3mm headphone jack. HumanDAC 36.6 HumanDAC 36.6 is a unique development by A.A. Balakhonsky, based on the ideology of preserving the maximum amount of information entering the DAC without subsequent processing. The goal of the project was to create a device that surpasses all existing counterparts in its honesty. The digital signal via I2S enters the very heart of the DAC — the Burr-Brown DAC8871 chip, which has an output voltage swing of 36.6 Volts, which is dozens of times higher than the standard values of other DACs. What does this mean in practice? It means that even the smallest details will not be lost in the signal path. This means that we will get a live, detailed, and real sound with the most natural reproduction of the surrounding space. In addition, HumanDAC 36.6 has another advantage — "bit-for-bit" conversion. Without "improvisation", "synthetics", "chemistry", and other "delights" of additional conversions and processing found in most modern DACs. The secret is that modern DACs have built-in algorithms for supplementing the analog signal in case of data loss. It is enough to lose one bit for the DAC to introduce something of its own while trying to "restore" the lost data block. It is important to note that all delta-sigma type DACs average up to thousands of samples to get one bit at the output. Project Details Project Ideologue: Alexander Balakhonsky Project Motto: "Natural sound for every music lover" Project Goal: To preserve the informational integrity of the musical signal during conversion from digital to analog space. Project Features  Unique, patented DAC. Patent RU2291555 Bit Perfect. Bit-to-bit. Sample-to-sample. No processing. Only what is in the input informational audio signal. Multibit R-2-R. Asynchronous. Independent operation of the left and right channels. Modular structure. Mono module. Dual mono for stereo. Possibility to connect any number of modules in parallel. Possibility to assemble any combination of modules.  Technical Specifications  Format of the input digital signal — I2S Support for sampling frequencies — from 0 to 1 MHz, any arbitrary frequency Format of the output analog signal — from 16 to 31 bits Peak-to-peak output voltage swing — 36.6 Volts Digital-to-analog conversion chip — Burr-Brown DAC8871  HumanDAC 36.6 Modules  Single — one chip in each channel. Upgrade to Double, Triple, Quad is available. Double — two chips in each channel. Upgrade to Triple, Quad is available. Triple — three chips in each channel. Upgrade to Quad is available. Quad — four chips in each channel. Single balance — two chips (1 plus and 1 minus) in each channel. Double balance — four chips (2 plus and 2 minus) in each channel. Single 31-bit — two chips (1 MSB and 1 LSB) in each channel. Double 31-bit — four chips (2 MSB and 2 LSB) in each channel.  HumanI2S 36.6 Modules  I2S switcher-buffer module without a controller Module with a controller  HumanBUF 36.6 Modules  V6 — a module with 6 isolated buffers with an output impedance of about 1 Ohm and an output voltage swing of 36.6 Volts.          Total Price* The price is for the base product only and does not include shipping or selected optional upgrades. To get a complete final quote, please submit your request to our consultant via email at shop@filinlabs.com or via Telegram at @RA_Fayzullin. We will send you an invoice & full costs calculation in the reply message.  Lead TimesYou can check the lead times for each item in the "Lead Times & Handcrafted Quality" section. If the standard waiting time does not suit you, you can request our expedited assembly service (for details, see the "Priority Assembly Option" section). We also remind you that installment payment options are available for any product (see the "Installments" section). Basic Configuration
