     t_onReady(function() {t_onFuncLoad('t491_init',function() {t491_init('2463201211');});}); #rec2463201211 .t-card__title{font-size:20px;font-family:var(--t-text-font,Arial);font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;}@media screen and (max-width:480px),(orientation:landscape) and (max-height:480px){#rec2463201211 .t-card__title{font-size:14px;}}#rec2463201211 .t-card__descr{font-size:20px;font-family:var(--t-text-font,Arial);}@media screen and (max-width:480px),(orientation:landscape) and (max-height:480px){#rec2463201211 .t-card__descr{font-size:14px;}}          Gerbera Sound Dual Mono Headphone AMP Total*: $1600 Buy Now    Key Features Specification     Pure Class A FET Architecture The core of the Dual Mono amplifier relies on hand-matched field-effect transistors (FETs) biased deeply into pure Class A. This circuit design mimics the fluid, organic midrange and sweet highs of legendary vacuum tubes while retaining the lightning-fast transient speed, tight bass control, and reliability of premium solid-state engineering. True Dual-Mono Separation Stereo crosstalk is entirely eradicated by allocating separate, independent power supply rails and discrete boards to each channel. This extreme level of physical and electrical isolation allows subtle ambient micro-details and instrument positioning to emerge with astonishing three-dimensional clarity. Nikitin Stepped Attenuator with Remote Control Unlike standard carbon volume potentiometers that introduce channel imbalance and compress dynamics, the volume level is managed by a high-precision Nikitin stepped ladder network. Using premium thin-film resistors and low-noise relays, it guarantees perfect channel matching down to the lowest listening levels and can be effortlessly controlled via a remote control suite. Delivering a massive 2x5 Watts of pure Class A power into a 32-Ohm load, it provides exceptional dynamic headroom. The amplifier is equipped with premium balanced (XLR) and unbalanced (RCA) inputs and outputs, managed by dedicated front-panel toggle switches. Volume attenuation and input routing are controlled via a high-precision Nikitin stepped resistor attenuator, fully operable via the included remote control. The unit is fully universal and optimized to drive any dynamic or planar magnetic headphones on the market, effortlessly handling impedances ranging from 8 to 600 Ohms.         Total Price* The price is for the base product only and does not include shipping or selected optional upgrades. To get a complete final quote, please submit your request to our consultant via email at shop@filinlabs.com or via Telegram at @RA_Fayzullin. We will send you an invoice & full costs calculation in the reply message.  Lead TimesYou can check the lead times for each item in the "Lead Times & Handcrafted Quality" section. If the standard waiting time does not suit you, you can request our expedited assembly service (for details, see the "Priority Assembly Option" section). We also remind you that installment payment options are available for any product (see the "Installments" section). Basic Configuration
  The standard configuration (base product) includes the stock product with no additional options.    
