     t_onReady(function() {t_onFuncLoad('t491_init',function() {t491_init('2462136601');});}); #rec2462136601 .t-card__title{font-size:20px;font-family:var(--t-text-font,Arial);font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;}@media screen and (max-width:480px),(orientation:landscape) and (max-height:480px){#rec2462136601 .t-card__title{font-size:14px;}}#rec2462136601 .t-card__descr{font-size:20px;font-family:var(--t-text-font,Arial);}@media screen and (max-width:480px),(orientation:landscape) and (max-height:480px){#rec2462136601 .t-card__descr{font-size:14px;}}          Gerbera Sound HA-15 Headphones Tube Amplifier Total*: $1800 Buy Now    Acoustic Signature Specification Connectivity & Upgrades     Unrivaled Technicality & Punch Despite being a tube amplifier, the HA-15 delivers a highly technical, collected, and punchy presentation. Second-order harmonics are present to add natural weight, but without any obvious or muddy distortion. The sound quality is directly comparable to the legendary Stax 700 series energizers, which cost exponentially more. Transformative Electrostatic Synergy When paired with the HA-15, electrostatic headphones like the HiFiMan Mini Shangri-La sound significantly more linear. High frequencies become breathtakingly resolving without any trace of sibilance or harshness (zero "treble peaking"). Classic models like the Koss ESP950 (used via adapter) are similarly transformed, showcasing massively improved frequency extremes and impact. Total Customization The HA-15 is built entirely to order. The standard configuration can be deeply modified according to your specific system needs. You can add or remove input/output connectors (e.g., swapping the 4.4mm for a 4-pin XLR) and completely redesign the front panel materials. The core standout feature of this amplifier is its immense versatility: the output stage delivers a robust 3 Watts of power via a 4.4mm balanced jack to effortlessly drive full-size planar magnetic and dynamic headphones. Simultaneously, it generates a massive 600V output via a dedicated Stax 5-pin connector for electrostatic earspeakers. Operating on the shortest possible signal path with zero global negative feedback (No NFB), the amplifier utilizes a pure single-stage topology with 6S15P (6С15П) vacuum tubes and authentic point-to-point hand-wiring.         Total Price* The price is for the base product only and does not include shipping or selected optional upgrades. To get a complete final quote, please submit your request to our consultant via email at shop@filinlabs.com or via Telegram at @RA_Fayzullin. We will send you an invoice & full costs calculation in the reply message.  Lead TimesYou can check the lead times for each item in the "Lead Times & Handcrafted Quality" section. If the standard waiting time does not suit you, you can request our expedited assembly service (for details, see the "Priority Assembly Option" section). We also remind you that installment payment options are available for any product (see the "Installments" section). Basic ConfigurationThe standard configuration (base product) includes the Gerbera Sound HA-15 Headphones Tube Amplifier with no additional options Amplifier TopologySingle-Ended, Single-Stage, Point-to-Point Wiring Global FeedbackZero Global Negative Feedback (No NFB) Vacuum Tubes1x 6S15P (6С15П) per channel Frequency Response10 Hz – 20,000 Hz Voltage Gain40 dB Input InterfaceUnbalanced RCA (50 kOhm Input Impedance) Output 1 (Planar/Dynamic)4.4mm Balanced | 3W Output Power | 8–100 Ohms Output 2 (Electrostatic)Stax Pro Bias 5-Pin | 600V Maximum Voltage TransformersCustom Moscow-wound Toroidal (TOR) Power & Output Warranty1 Year Comprehensive Factory Warranty         Stock: 4.4mm Balanced + Stax 5-Pin Pro   Custom: 4-Pin XLR Balanced + Stax 5-Pin Pro   Add Secondary Unbalanced 6.3mm Output  Add Secondary Analog RCA Input   Add Analog XLR Input   Vintage Tubes      
